            <ArticleTitle>Asthma in African Americans: what can we do about the higher rates of disease?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>193-201</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3949/ccjm.79a.11016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>African Americans not only have a higher prevalence of asthma than whites, they also are encumbered with higher rates of asthma-associated morbidity and death. Factors such as genetics, socioeconomic status, health maintenance behaviors, air quality, and obesity likely contribute in combination to these burdens. Further work is needed to better understand these complex risk factors. To remedy these disparities, we need to ensure that patients at higher risk are given proper care and the knowledge to control their asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
